{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792401867,"nonce":"FVa0i5jLVMn0qEtwp+1tqNggE0s=","title":"Extension manager: run built-in, user and workspace extensions in every project","message":"Part of the built-in extensions plan (see its umbrella issue). Blocks Git.\n\nToday one extension runs per project, in the Extension Studio, and only for a `.rayext` project. Installed extensions are listed and not run.\n\n- Discover: app `extensions/`, `~/.rayde/extensions`, `.rayde/extensions`. Same id in several places: workspace over user over built-in.\n- Activate on events from the config: `onStartup`, `workspaceContains:\u003cglob\u003e`, `onCommand:\u003cid\u003e`, `onView:\u003cid\u003e`. Nothing starts before its event.\n- One `rayscript-host` process each; log to a named Output channel; restart an extension that exits (at most three times a minute, then stay down and say so).\n- Merge contributions: commands (palette, `ext.\u003cid\u003e.\u003ccommand\u003e` key ids), menus, views (several extensions' icons in the activity bar; the sidebar shows one view at a time), settings sections named for the extension, key bindings.\n- Enable and disable per workspace and per user (`extensions.disabled` in settings); the Extensions page shows state, activation event, host status, capabilities, native libraries with path and hash, and a built-in marker.\n- Studio: opens the running extension's view and panels; a `.rayext` project replaces the same extension if it is running.\n- `describe` command convention for structured state.\n- Checks and a snapshot scenario: two extensions side by side, a crash and restart, disable.\n\nCurrent limits to lift: Workbench holds one `extension` and one Studio per main file; `Studio` is both the host connection and the development UI.","files":null}]}